1 NOTE {geni:about_me} • Emigration, to Dorset, MN, Abt 1930 - Clarkfield, Yellow Medicine County, MN, USA (?!!)
2 CONT
2 CONT Info from Bertha Jean Jorgenson: George married Brita Henriksdtr Stokkebo on Oct 28 1906 in Clarkfield, MN.  '''He was a blacksmith and did auto mechanic work besides farming'''.  My Dad , '''Hiram Wallace Jorgenson''', said he ha
2 CONC d a marvelous voice and once sang on the radio out of Fargo with Lawrence Welk before he was famous. The Eleven children:''' Marlow Herbert, Una Melvette, George Bertram, Helen Caroline, Harold Joseph, Leon Lincoln, Severin Alvin,
2 CONC  and Joan (Jo-an) Mavis.''' [remark.=8] Sept 11, 1918 Jorgen Severin Jorgenson registered for the draft WWI.  They moved from Clarkfield, MN. to Park Rapids after losing the farm. They purchased land from '''Clarence Severts''' fo
2 CONC r one dollar and other value considered.  His father: '''Mathias (Maurset) Jurgenson''' B: mar 26 1860. 
