1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Sebeka Review, June 6, 1947
2 CONT
2 CONT Two Men Meet Death By Suffocation In Jail At Frazee FRAZEE, MINN. - Two prisoners in the city jail here died of suffocation early Friday when bedding in their cell caught fire. The men were Arthur C. Mattson, 40 of Minneapolis, an
2 CONC d Alvin Knutson, 31, Fertile, both members of a nearby railroad construction crew.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chief of Police James Anderson said the two were being held on disorderly conduct charges after being arrested at Frazee Thursday night. They were believed to have been asphyxiated between 2 and 5 o'clok Friday morning when Charle
2 CONC s Turnbull, night policeman, was absent in Detroit Lakes checking on a stolen car. The men were in adjoining cells, in which the windows were found closed. Both victims were unmarried. Knutson leaves his father, Andrew Knutson of 
2 CONC Fertile, and two sisters. - Fergus Falls Daily Journal.
