1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Carl Helmer Lofthus was born in 1881 in Iowa.His parents were moving around Iowa after their marriage on July 7/1880 in Winnebago county before moving to the Winger area of Sletten, Polk county, Minnesota. As a res
2 CONC ult of this and after checking all counties in Iowa, Carl Helmer's birth was never registered in Iowa.This search was done by the Bureau of Health statistics in Des Moines, Iowa. Helmer and his brother Martin were hunting up in th
2 CONC e forest to the north, when Helmer got separated from Martin and he ended up freezing to death at 26 years old.This cemetery was plotted out in 1906/1907 and Carl Helmer Lofthus is the first burial in this cemetery on the Loftus p
2 CONC lot just on the south side of the church. The church was built in 1909 and Martin Loftus(Lofthus) was one of the founders and helped build this church.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/124798118/karl-helmer-loftus 
2 CONC Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 7 2020, 9:49:05 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl Helmer Lofthus was born in 1881 in Iowa.His parents were moving around Iowa after their marriage on July 7/1880 in Winnebago county before moving to the Winger area of Sletten, Polk county, Minnesota. As a result of this and 
2 CONC after checking all counties in Iowa, Carl Helmer's birth was never registered in Iowa.This search was done by the Bureau of Health statistics in Des Moines, Iowa.  Helmer and his brother Martin were hunting up in the forest to the
2 CONC  north, when Helmer got separated from Martin and he ended up freezing to death at 26 years old.This cemetery was plotted out in 1906/1907 and Carl Helmer Lofthus is the first burial in this cemetery on the Loftus plot just on the
2 CONC  south side of the church. The church was built in 1909 and Martin Loftus(Lofthus) was one of the founders and helped build this church.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/139923891/carl-helmer-lofthus Find A Grave M
