1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Therese Christiansen, 80, Cooperstown, died Sunday, Nov. 6, 2005, in her home under hospice care.
2 CONT
2 CONT Therese Fadness was born Sept. 26, 1925, near Sutton, N.D. She moved to the McHenry, N.D., area, where she graduated from high school in 1943. She received a teaching certificate from Valley City (N.D.) State University. She taugh
2 CONC t several years for area schools. On June 22, 1947, she married C.R. Christiansen in McHenry. They lived in McHenry, where they owned and operated Bob's Service and Independent Oil until 1985. He died in 1999.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by four sons, Robert (Mary), Jerome (Jane), both Casselton, N.D., Russell (Cheryl), New Rockford, N.D., John (Janice), Portland, N.D.; three daughters, Joan (Darryl) Anderson, Gillette, Wyo., Jill (Ed) Nesheim, Jam
2 CONC estown, N.D., An Christiansen, Plymouth, Minn.; four brothers, Russell (Clara), Fargo, Walter, Valley City, Don, Medford, Ore., Elton (Laurie), The Dalles, Ore.; 10 grandchildren and three great-grandchildren.
