1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ray was the son of Emil and Gessina (Williamson) Fadness. Ray graduated from Wolf Point, Mont. High School in 1935. He later moved to western Montana and married Florence Norman in 1941.
2 CONT
2 CONT He worked at various jobs including Fort Peck Dam in Montana, the Ammunition Depot at Hermiston, Ore. and the shipyards at Tacoma. He entered the United States Army in 1945 and received his honorable discharge in 1946 and returned
2 CONC  to Hamilton, Mont. In 1948 the Fadness family moved to Sunnyside and Ray joined the Iron Workers Union and worked at the Hanford Project until he retired in 1979.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ray was a member of Calvary Lutheran Church in Sunnyside.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his wife of 57 years, Florence, two children, Doug and wife, Pam and Dolores Tadlock Gilles and husband, Lee; former son-in-law, Larry Tadlock; a sister, Maisie Petri; five brothers, Bud,Stan, Milton, Vern, and M
2 CONC el; six grandchildren, Krista, Karia, Ryan, and Megan Fadness, Shane and Kyle Tadlock; two great-grandchildren; three sisters-in-law, Jean Warner and husband, Clayton, Velma Hargraves and Betty Chaon; two brothers-in-law, Ted Norm
2 CONC an and wife, Betty, and Dan Norman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ray died at his home following a courageous battle with cancer.
