1 OCCU Ironworker
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Melbourne Vincent Fadness BIRTH	21 Mar 1932 Wolf Point, Roosevelt County, Montana, USA DEATH	8 Jun 2013 (aged 81) Butte, Silver Bow County, Montana, USA BURIAL	Unknown  MEMORIAL ID	112297196 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 0 FLOWERS 2 Melbourne Vincent Fadness passed away peacefully on Saturday, June 8, 2013, surrounded by his children and their spouses.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mel was born in Wolf Point, Mont., on March 21, 1932, the ninth of 10 children to Emil and Gessina (Williamson) Fadness. He spent most of his childhood in the Bitterroot and graduated from Darby High School.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was drafted into the Army in 1952 and served in Germany. He married Colleen McCarthy in 1957 and raised their five children while working in the Ironworkers Union and then at the Smelter.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the Smelter closed he began working at Montana State Hospital at Warm Springs.
2 CONT
2 CONT He loved fishing and camping and later in life became an avid reader and sports fan. He loved to watch baseball, football and his beloved Grizzlies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mel loved J.A. Jance mysteries, Montana and Indian history.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mel was preceded in death by his parents, seven siblings, his wife, Colleen, and son, Dale.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by children, Scott (Debbie), Lee (Debbie), Lynn (Steve) Reid, Tod (Dannette); and his brothers, Stan (Jan) and Vern (Sandy). He was blessed with eight grandchildren and eight great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT At Mel's request funeral services will not be held. In lieu of flowers the family requests donations in Mel's name to the Hearst Free Library or Pintler Pets.
2 CONT
2 CONT Axelson Alternative Cremation is privileged to serve the Fadness Family.
2 CONT
