1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Father was Albert Sigurd Carlson, Sr.; mother was Ingeborg Okland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grave: https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/43776585/albert-sigurd-carlson
2 CONT Fina a Grave obit;
2 CONT Albert Carlson, 66, of Park Rapids, died Wednesday May 2, 1984 at the Methodist Hospital in Rochester.
2 CONT He was born May 22, 1917 to Albert and Ingeborg Carlson in N.Y. His parents died when he was very young, so in 1924 he moved to Dorset to live with his uncle, Hans Arvik. Later he moved to Park Rapids where he was raised to manhoo
2 CONC d by the Dan Buss family. Attended schools in the Park Rapids area graduating from the Park Rapids High School in 1934. On July 4, 1937 he married Helen Jorgenson in Park Rapids, where the couple made their home until moving to th
2 CONC e Iron Range in 1951. He retired in 1980 when he and his wife returned to Park Rapids and has made his home here since.
2 CONT Survivors include his wife, Helen of Park Rapids, two sons, Robert of Butte, MT and Danny who is stationed with the Army at Ft. Levenworth, KS; six daughters, Mrs. Wayne (Nancy) Harris of San Francisco, CA, Mrs. Gary (Janet) Erchu
2 CONC l of Ely, Mrs. George (Mary) Yapel of Virginia, Mrs. James H. (Elizabeth) Pearson of Duluth, Mrs. Tom (Marlys) Trembath of Chisholm and Mrs. Paul Dennis of Park Rapids; two sisters Mrs. Emily Wood of Brick, N. Jand Mrs. Kenneth (E
2 CONC dna)Peterson of Bohemia, N.Y.; 21 grandchildren, two great grandchildren and several nieces and nephews. He was preceded in death by his parents and one brother Arthur.
2 CONT Funeral services were held at 10:00 am Saturday May 5 at Calvary Lutheran church in Park Rapids, with the Rev. Allan Oman officiating. Organist was Julie Olson and soloist was Palmer Vaadeland who sang "The Old Rugged Cross" and "
2 CONC In the Garden.
2 CONT Active Pallbearers were Patrick Erchul, Michael Yapel, A. B. (Bucky) Boeringer, Jeffrey Mickelson, Steven Mickelson, and Benjamin Pickett, Jr.
2 CONT Interment was in Greenwood Cemetery with arrangements handled by the Jones-Behrens Funeral Home of Park Rapids.
2 CONT Park Rapids Enterprise May 5, 1984
